\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Length on the diagonal line}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{H=\{(s,s):s\in\mathbb R\}} with the inner product
inherited from #{\mathbb R^2}. Its unit vector is #{(1,1)/\sqrt2}.
The [induced Euclidean measure](fdip-002M) of the segment #{0\le s\le1}
is #{\sqrt2}: its orthonormal coordinate runs from zero to #{\sqrt2}.
Its ambient area is zero, since each vertical section is empty or a singleton
and nonnegative Tonelli applies to the Borel product. Its raw
#{s}-coordinate length is #{1}. Thus the basis vector #{(1,1)} requires
a volume factor #{\sqrt2}.}
\p{The length calculation uses the orthonormal-chart characterization
of [induced measure](fdip-002M). The section argument is the
sigma-finite Borel Tonelli theorem,
\citet{Theorem 1.7.15, pp. 200-201, preliminary version}{tao2011measure}.}
